* FD-19  Common-mode feedback transient (spec 3.1.2: drive the input common
* mode as far as the application allows and check the output common mode
* stays at its design value).  The FD-01 network's common-mode source steps
* VCOM -> VCOM + {{CM_STEP}} V -> VCOM; the output common-mode deviation,
* its settling and any ringing show the CMFB loop's stability.
{{SEED_OPTION}}
.lib "{{MODEL_LIB}}" {{CORNER}}
{{MC_PARAM}}
.include "{{DUT_FILE}}"
.temp {{TEMP}}
.options reltol=1e-6 abstol=1e-15 vntol=1e-9 method=gear
VDD vdd 0 {{VDD}}
VSS vss 0 0
IBIAS vdd ibias {{IBIAS}}
VCM vcm 0 {{VCM}}
VI vi vcm PULSE(0 {{CM_STEP}} {{T_DELAY}} {{T_EDGE}} {{T_EDGE}} {{T_WIDTH}} {{T_PERIOD}})
R1 vi inp {{R_NET}}
R2 inp outn {{R_NET}}
R3 vi inn {{R_NET}}
R4 inn outp {{R_NET}}
XDUT vss ibias vdd vcmpin inp inn outp outn {{DUT}}
RVCM_DUT vcm vcmpin 1k
RLP outp vcm {{RL}}
CLP outp 0 {{CL}}
RLN outn vcm {{RL}}
CLN outn 0 {{CL}}
.control
set filetype=ascii
tran {{TSTEP}} {{TSTOP}} 0 {{TMAX}}
write {{RAW}} v(outp) v(outn)
.endc
.end
